WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.583
Open the Office page and choose Activate only.

00:00:03.583 --> 00:00:08.667
This command targets the volume licensed edition described on the page.

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:12.042
It does not apply to every Office edition.

00:00:12.042 --> 00:00:16.250
Make sure you already have a valid Office volume license.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:22.042
A generic key is not a purchased license and cannot activate a personal retail copy.

00:00:22.042 --> 00:00:26.750
This step contacts the third-party service identified on the page.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:32.042
Choose PowerShell or CMD to match the administrator terminal you will open.

00:00:32.042 --> 00:00:35.167
You are selecting a command format.

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:38.500
The website does not perform activation.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.625
Click Copy full command and check the website feedback.

00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:46.250
If copying fails, download the text.

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:52.000
Keep the complete command, including its key, verification and error checks.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.375
Paste into the matching administrator terminal.

00:00:55.375 --> 00:00:59.583
Read and check the content before deciding whether to run it.

00:00:59.583 --> 00:01:05.083
This is only an illustration and neither shows nor promises successful activation.

00:01:05.083 --> 00:01:09.042
Check the actual license status of the target edition.

00:01:09.042 --> 00:01:12.917
Another licensed edition does not prove success.

00:01:12.917 --> 00:01:18.500
Stop and investigate errors, an unlicensed status or an unreachable service.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.208
Starting a command is not proof of activation.
